  "body": "Goal: The 3D tool preview shows helical flutes on the revolved model of a tool.\n\nReason: The user wants to see the flutes in the 3D model preview. #3894 adds an orbitable 3D model to the tool library window. A tool without an imported body shows a mesh that is revolved from its profile. That mesh has no flutes.\n\nData that is available:\n- The tool stores `flutes`.\n- The catalog facts store `catalog.helix_deg`.\n\nWork:\n- Cut helical grooves into the fluted length of the revolved display mesh. Use `flutes` for the number of grooves and `catalog.helix_deg` for the helix angle. Use a straight flute when the helix angle is not known.\n- The fluted mesh is for display only.\n\nSafety rule:\n- The collision, gouge and verify checks must NOT read the fluted mesh. They keep the conservative revolved envelope.\n- A test must pin this rule. For example: a check on a tool gives the same result before and after the fluted display mesh is built.\n\nFrame cost (`crates/ui/AGENTS.md`): cache the fluted mesh on its inputs (the tool value, the helix angle, the flute count). A still frame computes no mesh.\n\nDepends on: #3894.\n\nPart of #3663.\n\nDone means: the 3D preview of a fluted tool without a body shows helical grooves on the fluted length. A pinning test shows that no check reads the fluted mesh.\n\nLabels: this account cannot set labels. A collaborator, please set the labels. Suggested: `P6`, `effort:medium`, `enhancement`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n",
